{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-13T16:33:08.298Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"1f65549d969a385dd658b1e6","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1706","claim:pm-gh1716","claim:pm-jndg9a","lineage:pm-jndg9a","lineage:pm-998juj","lineage:pm-u9d0","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-gh1706+pm-gh1716+pm-jndg9a","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1706","claim:pm-gh1716","claim:pm-jndg9a","lineage:pm-jndg9a","lineage:pm-998juj","lineage:pm-u9d0","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.323","source":"probe"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-v1mp64"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"A passing pm test --run row echoes the command's full stdout, including raw ANSI colour codes, so every quiet pass grows with the runner's report"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Found while recording linked-test evidence for the note-conflict fix (2026-11-13). pm test --run keeps each run_results row's complete captured stdout and stderr even when the command passed, the context matched and the run was trusted. A vitest-based linked test prints its coloured summary, so a passing two-file run returns 694 B of stdout of which 304 B are ANSI escape sequences (JSON response 2,697 B in total); in TOON the same stdout is one escaped string cell. The reply grows with the runner's report (file count, test names) although an agent only needs the verdict on a quiet pass, and the escape sequences are noise in every encoding. The decision-field projection added for the execution context leaves stdout untouched. Proposal: on a passing, trusted, mismatch-free row, keep a bounded tail of stdout with ANSI sequences removed (or a byte count with a restore selector), keep full output on failing, refused and mismatched rows, and let an explicit selector (for example --full-output) restore it. Duplicate check: searched linked test run stdout ANSI escape passing output, and run_results stdout passing run bounded output; the closed bounded test-run summaries task persists summaries on item records but does not shape the command reply."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["agent-ux","linked-tests","token-efficiency"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-11-13T16:33:08.298Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-13T16:33:08.298Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":90},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"A passing, trusted, mismatch-free pm test --run row returns no raw ANSI escape sequences and at most a bounded stdout tail in TOON and JSON; Failing, refused, skipped and mismatched rows keep their full captured output; An explicit selector restores the full output on every row, and the omission receipt names it"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-5t33or"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"low"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/severity","value":"low"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"A passing trusted linked-test row returns its verdict and at most a bounded, escape-free tail of stdout"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"A passing row returns the command's full stdout with raw ANSI colour codes"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-gh1716","kind":"discovered_from","created_at":"2026-11-13T16:33:08.298Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-tcvccz","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-11-13T16:33:08.298Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"6cc70f3e99346a7ec95a12cf34b4e104da325d36f0c2918b1fd058249e005e87","item_hash_version":3,"message":"","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"2cdeda1eb46977f06dc93da606c1437152043f6aa94449717649cc8866b1f887"}
