{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-13T19:40:41.858Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"bde39398f74f9316857947fc","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-tcvccz","claim:pm-v1mp64","lineage:pm-v1mp64","lineage:pm-5t33or","lineage:pm-n7rr","lineage:pm-mpbb","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-tcvccz+pm-v1mp64","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-tcvccz","claim:pm-v1mp64","lineage:pm-v1mp64","lineage:pm-5t33or","lineage:pm-n7rr","lineage:pm-mpbb","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.323","source":"probe"}},"op":"note_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-13T19:40:41.858Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/notes","value":[{"created_at":"2026-11-13T19:40:41.858Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Design (2026-11-13): stream bounding uses the same quiet-run gate as the context projection. When a run is quiet, each row whose trust is not false keeps an escape-free tail of stdout and stderr. The tail strips escapes with node:util stripVTControlCharacters, keeps only the final segment of each carriage-return overwrite, drops blank lines, and holds at most 6 lines and 480 code points. A shortened stream adds `<stream>_omitted_bytes` to its row (UTF-8 bytes of the original minus the tail). The reply's omission_receipt gains `run_results.stdout` / `run_results.stderr` (test-all: `results.run_results.*`) with restore_with `--full-output`, appended after any groups the reply already declares.\n\nThe following rows keep their complete streams: failing, refused, skipped and mismatched rows; every row of a non-quiet run; and a row that passed only under an explicit untrusted-command override. That last row's output is what a reviewer reads before trusting the command.\n\n`--full-output` is a presentation-only selector on pm test (requires --run) and pm test-all. It is independent of `--check-context`, which restores contexts only.\n\nMeasured on a vitest-style two-line ANSI report: the stdout cell drops 17 B of escapes. A real 3-file vitest report keeps the 6 summary lines (Test Files / Tests / Start at / Duration plus the last two file lines)."}]}],"before_hash":"0915a41324fdd2e1636347d3b7f3b39ae6da630e512973ce28efb48a2410acf1","after_hash":"352bd64ece9ca2e8ef3691100ae5df84716bc40bd8ffc80d485400ef41801a66","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"db87573ee5ed5feb4f48fc01d35f33154e4a1207fdbd8387c34227cbfb92c3c8"}
